hatlog space whether it contains many lines or no text.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:27:`ActionPopupBottomRow` is a separate popup footer after the scroll body. It uses `background.default`, a top border, and popup-wide padding, which creates the gray bar below the prompt. It owns usage information and Finish, Schedule, Send, Run, and Stop controls. Command actions have no visible prompt surface, so their Run row must remain standalone.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:32:- Make the prompt surface a column with three regions: scrollable editor, optional predefined phrases, and `ActionPopupBottomRow` as a non-scrolling footer. Sticky means the footer remains visible at the surface bottom while editor content scrolls; it does not require CSS `position: sticky`.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:38:- Subscribe to prompt text at the smallest component that changes prompt height or resize availability. Do not hoist draft updates into `ActionPopupContent`, because chatlog and unrelated popup content must not rerender for each keystroke.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:43:- Given an empty or whitespace-only agent prompt, its editable region is one line high and the chatlog receives the released vertical space.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_2\\\\B_009_running_agents_visibility.md:3:title: running-agents indicator misses action and onState runs\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_2\\\\B_009_running_agents_visibility.md:15:Only some conversation paths register in the global running list. Manual, state-triggered, scheduled, command, agent, and continuation runs can therefore disagree across the shell indicator, card, popup, and conversation panel.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_2\\\\B_009_running_agents_visibility.md:27:- Starting any action increments the global running count until Electron reports a terminal execution state.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_2\\\\B_009_running_agents_visibility.md:35:- `design\\\\architecture\\\\initial description\\\\writings\\\\running_actions.md`\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_0_4\\\\F_96_ctrl_enter_on_action_input.md:23:- Prevent default behavior and stop propagation, then flush the latest prompt before running the existing shortcut callback.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:5:title: Improve agent selectors on action popup\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:32:The selector row appears above agent conversation content. `ActionPopupBottomRow` separately renders the usage controls on the left and run controls on the right. Settings already persist through `ActionRunSettingsStore`; selectors stay disabled while settings load or a run is queued or running, but remain editable while an agent waits for input.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:37:- Remove selector rendering from `ActionPopupContent`. Render it only for agent actions in `ActionPopupBottomRow`, before the centered usage group. Lay out selectors left, the existing `tokens`, `changes`, and `lines` controls centered as one group, and run controls right. Keep all groups usable without horizontal overflow when popup width is constrained.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:40:- Keep selectors disabled while settings load or run status is `queued` or `running`. Keep them enabled during `waitingForInput`; changes then retain `settingsChangedWhileWaiting` so next send applies restarted settings.\\ndesign\\\\releases\\\\0_2_0\\\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:46:- Agent action popup bottom row shows model selector first on left, usage controls centered, and action buttons on right; selector no longer appears above conversation content.\\ndesign\\\\releas